{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 104, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning a missing node2->node3 edge into a skip adds a new path to the output (exp 16, +13 to +19), so the gain should be larger than when it replaces an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Putting parameter-free pooling in place of a convolution on the direct input->output edge loses capacity (exp 20, -7 to -14)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where the direct input->output edge was empty creates a new learnable path to the output (exp 11 fits)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 3 is already empty, removing edge 4 leaves the output depending on edge 5 alone (exp 4, IN16 -16.9)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv into the output should cost more than deleting a skip, which can sometimes help (exp 1)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv into the output with pooling removes the cell's main learnable path (by the general conv-vs-pool pattern; untested here)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2 empty, node 2 is fed only by edge 1, so making that edge a pool degrades the whole node-2 branch (exp 13 fits)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where the node1->node2 edge was empty adds depth and capacity, which should help more than swapping out an existing op (untested here)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 4 is empty, the direct edge carries more of the output, so making it a strong conv should matter more (untested here)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv into the output with a parameter-free skip loses capacity, whereas filling an empty edge 4 does not (untested here)."}], "tok": 7984, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [1, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [4, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [1, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none"], [5, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [2, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [1, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1",